{"text": "Kwon Castellano & Associates, P.C.                                       W/P ref. R-2\nClient: Varga Precision Castings, Inc. (\"VPC\")                 FYE 12/31/2025\nSubject: Related party transactions (AU-C 550 / ASC 850)\nPrepared: I. Castellano 02/18/2026        Reviewed: HJK 02/24/2026\n\nOBJECTIVE\nIdentify related parties, test completeness of management's list (PBC item 41), and\nevaluate whether transactions are disclosed and at terms we can describe.\n\nRELATED PARTIES IDENTIFIED\n(a) Anselm Varga -- founder, CEO, 62% shareholder.\n(b) Katalin Varga-Thorne -- his daughter, VP Operations, 19% shareholder.\n(c) Desmond Thorne -- Katalin's husband. Sole member of Thorne Logistics Group, LLC (\"TLG\").\n    NOT on management's list. Found via vendor master: TLG's remit address is\n    77 Quarry Hollow Road, Lewisburg, PA 17837 -- same as Katalin's home address in HR file.\n(d) VPC Hungary Kft. -- 100% sub, Gyor. Managing director Felix Baumgartner-Ruiz.\n(e) Blue Juniata Lake House LLC -- owned by Mr. Varga personally. See item 4.\n\nTRANSACTIONS TESTED\n1. Freight paid to TLG: $1,284,300 (2024: $402,150). Tripled. No bids obtained. Traced\n   12 invoices; rates run 18-22% above the two carriers VPC used before. Controller says\n   \"Des is reliable.\" Proposed: disclose; discuss with audit committee.\n2. Intercompany: VPC wired EUR 640,000 to the sub on 14 March 2025. Booked as loan, no\n   note on file. Beneficiary account IBAN FR58 5640 7655 8395 8814 5082 902 -- that is a FRENCH\n   IBAN, not Hungarian. Baumgartner-Ruiz says the sub banks in Lyon \"for convenience.\"\n   Requested bank confirmation direct. Form 5472 n/a (VPC is the US parent) but confirm w/ tax.\n3. Shareholder loan to Mr. Varga: opening balance $350,000; advances $125,000 on 6/2/2025 and\n   $90,000 on 10/20/2025; no repayments; closing $565,000. Interest accrued at 4%,\n   not paid. Advances went by wire from the Susquehanna Heritage Bank operating account\n   (xxxxxx4093) to his personal account 7782-0-116459.\n4. Lake house: VPC paid $48,600 of \"customer entertainment facility\" costs to Blue Juniata\n   Lake House LLC, incl. dock repair and a pontoon (the \"Molten Lady\"). Usage log shows\n   3 customer events and 41 family days. Personal use >> business. Proposed AJE to\n   reclass to shareholder loan; tax to consider constructive dividend.\n5. Political: $10,000 check #20417 dated 9/30/2025 to Friends of Varga for County Commissioner,\n   coded to \"dues & subscriptions.\" Mr. Varga is the candidate. Corporate contribution; non-\n   deductible; legal exposure -- refer to counsel. Controller unaware it was an issue.\n\nOTHER\n- Ms. Varga-Thorne signed the management rep letter draft for related parties. Given (c),\n  Hye-jin Kwon wants the CEO and the board chair to sign instead.\n- Per HR, Mr. Thorne was a VPC employee until 2022; terminated after a positive drug test.\n  Not relevant to the financial statements; do not carry forward.\n\nCONCLUSION\nManagement's list incomplete. Items 1, 3, 4 require disclosure. Item 5 communicated to\nthose charged with governance 2/26/2026. Passed adjustment schedule updated.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "460 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Anselm Varga", "Katalin Varga-Thorne", "Desmond Thorne", "Felix Baumgartner-Ruiz", "Des", "Mr. Varga", "Mr. Thorne", "Ms. Varga-Thorne", "Hye-jin Kwon"], "companies": ["Kwon Castellano & Associates, P.C.", "Varga Precision Castings, Inc.", "Blue Juniata Lake House LLC", "Thorne Logistics Group, LLC", "VPC Hungary Kft.", "TLG", "VPC", "Susquehanna Heritage Bank", "Friends of Varga"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.30000000074505806, "modelMs": 36708, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections"